    "lesson": {
      "title": "Nutrients & plant growth",
      "instruction": "Compare nutrient-limited growth with a balanced reference, holding light and water fixed.",
      "explanation": "Light and water are fixed and suitable. All supplies are relative levels; 100 is sufficient in this fictional plant. Biomass follows the lowest supply up to a ceiling of 100. Height is a separate nonlinear index. Equal shortages co-limit growth. Deficiency cues are illustrative. Excess, soil interactions, species differences and toxicity are outside this teaching model; it is not fertilizer advice."
